  "implemented": [
    "Exactly the four existing host launches publish an atomic random nonce bound to isolated package/build/phase/previous passed run. OS Settings Back does not publish another nonce.",
    "IsolateNameServer synchronous atomic registration admits one process owner before report/SQL/widget work. Cross-isolate duplicate receives only a bounded challenge-bound identity ping, emits diagnostics and returns without business/report/ack writes.",
    "Owner port remains registered after passed or failed. Silence, wrong challenge, wrong identity or different nonce never authorizes a replacement owner.",
    "Cross-PID resume requires the saved checkpoint with the exact same host authorization and original absolute deadline; same runId and exact SQL/model comparisons remain mandatory.",
    "Any retained failed or unfinished run is refused across build/nonce changes; first error and rejected report are preserved. Only a passed valid phase predecessor can authorize a fresh host run.",
    "Raw running/failed/passed observations use distinct status-bearing filenames; a later failure at the same stage cannot overwrite its first running raw report.",
    "Lifecycle/entry diagnostics and Android lifecycle logcat tags added; real channel observations saved before enabled/disabled assertions."
  ],
